[{:db/id "q-279719/field-1/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "0b7a3340-41fc-5696-8019-130372fdf579" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279719/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8edf95a-9a43-5579-83a2-b4923ea3a48e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279719/field-1/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer-field/choices ["q-279719/field-1/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279719/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "f4a94b74-8629-5955-a633-816136e55aa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279719/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bf7da68-b2e1-5f1f-bf22-803ac2314ada" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279719/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-279719/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279719" :question/id #uuid "8785ebc4-cb18-57c0-a373-6234a7edbb89" :question/math-academy-id "q-279719" :question/problem "Determine the lengths of the major and minor axes of the ellipse whose equation is $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+12x-4y=-20.$\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we must group the $x$ terms and the $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+12x-4y & =-20 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+12x)+({y}^{2}-4y) & =-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}^{2}+12x)+({y}^{2}-4y) & =-20 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}+6x)+({y}^{2}-4y) & =-20 \\\\ 2[(x+3)^{2}-9]+[(y-2)^{2}-4] & =-20 \\\\ 2(x+3)^{2}-18+(y-2)^{2}-4 & =-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+3)^{2}-18+(y-2)^{2}-4 & =-20 \\\\ 2(x+3)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =-20+18+4 \\\\ 2(x+3)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{1}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\sqrt{2}>1,$ the length of the major axis  $=2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=2\\sqrt{2},$ and the length of the minor axis  $=2\\cdot 1=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279719/field-1" "q-279719/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d21d6066-f7c8-5a47-b150-d0ae25d2d60b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279719"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7632/selection/c1d3aef88b1fb7ecf3fddb51dcad568a6bd266e00ada20f42f03e60154928af1" :answer/id #uuid "b218dd06-24b6-509a-b979-9c20acc228f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7632/selection/e73aa922030024cfbd6ec7d56544b6ec3ea62ba5b9daa177261b64205e381b1a" :answer/id #uuid "27fa5f16-e347-53a5-a3c4-f4f6ae612e92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7632/selection/3daf7c7813fd10d96af0e7397ad761fd8013a7868d9b6c8ad4b2e20ce2d33dca" :answer/id #uuid "2f0800d1-163a-50ba-b55d-483d45169160" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7632/selection/8fbd2d3f8fec30b8988b313ab55584eaf14bae431349fa2771dc259291903d20" :answer/id #uuid "8d00ecb1-0d31-560c-8fb8-1c69998a9f3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7632/selection/7a5aab969ffcdbe5ac6bd1a68897506c93bac105dd752828cf140c8ec9e1f647" :answer/id #uuid "78799a76-f02d-5742-85bc-3785656ee7ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7632/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7a44d67-f7b4-56de-abfc-56f9231d6993" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7632/selection/7a5aab969ffcdbe5ac6bd1a68897506c93bac105dd752828cf140c8ec9e1f647" :answer-field/choices ["q-7632/selection/c1d3aef88b1fb7ecf3fddb51dcad568a6bd266e00ada20f42f03e60154928af1" "q-7632/selection/e73aa922030024cfbd6ec7d56544b6ec3ea62ba5b9daa177261b64205e381b1a" "q-7632/selection/3daf7c7813fd10d96af0e7397ad761fd8013a7868d9b6c8ad4b2e20ce2d33dca" "q-7632/selection/8fbd2d3f8fec30b8988b313ab55584eaf14bae431349fa2771dc259291903d20" "q-7632/selection/7a5aab969ffcdbe5ac6bd1a68897506c93bac105dd752828cf140c8ec9e1f647"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7632" :question/id #uuid "d89c8157-fdbf-5abc-9fc7-e08ea29025fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-7632" :question/problem "Determine the center of the ellipse whose equation is $5{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-10x-36y=4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must group the $x$ terms and the $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-10x-36y & =4 \\\\ (5{x}^{2}-10x)+(9{y}^{2}-36y) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5{x}^{2}-10x)+(9{y}^{2}-36y) & =4 \\\\ 5[{x}^{2}-2x]+9[{y}^{2}-4y] & =4 \\\\ 5[(x-1)^{2}-{1}^{2}]+9[(y-2)^{2}-{2}^{2}] & =4 \\\\ 5[(x-1)^{2}-1]+9[(y-2)^{2}-4] & =4 \\\\ 5(x-1)^{2}-5+9(y-2)^{2}-36 & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x-1)^{2}-5+9(y-2)^{2}-36 & =4 \\\\ 5(x-1)^{2}+9(y-2)^{2} & =4+5+36 \\\\ 5(x-1)^{2}+9(y-2)^{2} & =45 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{5} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse is centered at $(1,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7632/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d21d6066-f7c8-5a47-b150-d0ae25d2d60b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7632"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115314/selection/93fb82ac5f7f057f85da1fe86c7a963325ca548ec91a734e7ea380e050beb566" :answer/id #uuid "b31ecabd-f887-572b-990d-86ebc62eb1eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(6,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115314/selection/87afcf1f52d3c7a155a8fed03dd6141198cb280e8a8412a016fff34fc30d942f" :answer/id #uuid "dc532de6-ff41-5bda-82f8-33ff0aa394e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115314/selection/036aea2a22728e00f002a3663dc7c52238513c28652c42149da20e1d2f70e918" :answer/id #uuid "908681d4-5f25-5951-889f-26e9e13164c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-6,-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115314/selection/21eec4a334619c06d7c7b7bf3003b8ceed360379ce8ec7fdfc876115d514eea1" :answer/id #uuid "2ca17eca-d557-5b5d-971a-cb88d7aeccd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,2\\sqrt{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115314/selection/778c353184dc2f90b9c60c504f37ad8f6d048fa9753af8c9158889f74a47bc06" :answer/id #uuid "673e58c0-cb8b-5547-b18f-d01aa08916b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-4,-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115314/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "28c0d1c1-846e-58ea-859c-cd4bd00a45dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115314/selection/036aea2a22728e00f002a3663dc7c52238513c28652c42149da20e1d2f70e918" :answer-field/choices ["q-115314/selection/93fb82ac5f7f057f85da1fe86c7a963325ca548ec91a734e7ea380e050beb566" "q-115314/selection/87afcf1f52d3c7a155a8fed03dd6141198cb280e8a8412a016fff34fc30d942f" "q-115314/selection/036aea2a22728e00f002a3663dc7c52238513c28652c42149da20e1d2f70e918" "q-115314/selection/21eec4a334619c06d7c7b7bf3003b8ceed360379ce8ec7fdfc876115d514eea1" "q-115314/selection/778c353184dc2f90b9c60c504f37ad8f6d048fa9753af8c9158889f74a47bc06"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115314" :question/id #uuid "e8fdb3e7-9493-53f7-a6c7-da3464300fc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-115314" :question/problem "Determine the center of the ellipse whose equation is $3{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+36x+32y=-124.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must group the $x$ terms and the $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+36x+32y & =-124 \\\\ (3{x}^{2}+36x)+(4{y}^{2}+32y) & =-124\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3{x}^{2}+36x)+(4{y}^{2}+32y) & =-124 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}+12x]+4[{y}^{2}+8y] & =-124 \\\\ 3[(x+6)^{2}-{6}^{2}]+4[(y+4)^{2}-{4}^{2}] & =-124 \\\\ 3[(x+6)^{2}-36]+4[(y+4)^{2}-16] & =-124 \\\\ 3(x+6)^{2}-108+4(y+4)^{2}-64 & =-124\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+6)^{2}-108+4(y+4)^{2}-64 & =-124 \\\\ 3(x+6)^{2}+4(y+4)^{2} & =-124+108+64 \\\\ 3(x+6)^{2}+4(y+4)^{2} & =48 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse is centered at $(-6,-4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115314/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d21d6066-f7c8-5a47-b150-d0ae25d2d60b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115314"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "a96070ff-745d-5d5f-9ed9-f6c3fe9d3d09" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "cd5e9908-3a0e-5c6b-b28f-45ca7675a20b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "d3ea0c7d-446d-50ec-ab8f-5f42863446b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "0e142be1-47bf-57d8-8644-1024e05909b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "509c36c9-25ff-5186-8cc4-149768146f78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "26b3adea-5150-5978-81f3-967d46b5391b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7639/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-7639/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-7639/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-7639/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-7639/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-7639/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7639" :question/id #uuid "fd2cdae2-5e26-5778-ab7e-65d79d794e32" :question/math-academy-id "q-7639" :question/problem "Consider the ellipse whose equation is ${x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2x+12y=-11.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Its center is $(1,-3)$\n- The length of the major axis  is $2\\sqrt{2}$\n- The length of the minor axis is $4$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must group the $x$ and $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2x+12y & =-11 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+(2{y}^{2}+12y) & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-2x)+(2{y}^{2}+12y) & =-11 \\\\ [{x}^{2}-2x]+2[{y}^{2}+6y] & =-11 \\\\ [(x-1)^{2}-{1}^{2}]+2[(y+3)^{2}-{3}^{2}] & =-11 \\\\ [(x-1)^{2}-1]+2[(y+3)^{2}-9] & =-11 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+2(y+3)^{2}-18 & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}-1+2(y+3)^{2}-18 & =-11 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+2(y+3)^{2} & =-11+1+18 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+2(y+3)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2\\sqrt{2}>2,$ the length of the major axis is $2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}=4\\sqrt{2},$ the length of the minor axis is $2\\cdot 2=4,$ and the ellipse is centered at $(1,-3).$\n\nTherefore,  I and III are true, and II is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-7639/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d21d6066-f7c8-5a47-b150-d0ae25d2d60b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7639"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279720/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "c2509930-fb41-5e8a-9e8b-3bd10e6c818d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279720/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6086bdbd-179f-5a28-9100-144742508193" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279720/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-279720/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279720/field-2/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "01011493-6cd4-5622-a783-94fdde12035d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279720/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b6f5408-73f8-5bea-8ff5-67cbab6755aa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279720/field-2/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-279720/field-2/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279720" :question/id #uuid "bf625522-510b-5214-b5b1-c05f88af5732" :question/math-academy-id "q-279720" :question/problem "Determine the lengths of the major and minor axes of the ellipse whose equation is $4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-16x+18y=119.$\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we must group the $x$ terms and the $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-16x+18y & =119 \\\\ (4{x}^{2}-16x)+(9{y}^{2}+18y) & =119\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4{x}^{2}-16x)+(9{y}^{2}+18y) & =119 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-4x)+9({y}^{2}+2y) & =119 \\\\ 4[(x-2)^{2}-4]+9[(y+1)^{2}-1] & =119 \\\\ 4(x-2)^{2}-16+9(y+1)^{2}-9 & =119\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-2)^{2}-16+9(y+1)^{2}-9 & =119 \\\\ 4(x-2)^{2}+9(y+1)^{2} & =119+16+9 \\\\ 4(x-2)^{2}+9(y+1)^{2} & =144 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{6}^{2}}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $6>4,$ the length of the major axis  $=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the length of the minor axis  $=2\\cdot 4=8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279720/field-1" "q-279720/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d21d6066-f7c8-5a47-b150-d0ae25d2d60b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279720"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115316/selection/7a5aab969ffcdbe5ac6bd1a68897506c93bac105dd752828cf140c8ec9e1f647" :answer/id #uuid "ae38466b-d76b-5e75-be7c-aec6d761cc2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115316/selection/f2b3d4b1886cc4c3079a0c9268e27d63493239a5d6ef9ca8c4a6ace4d05e3e97" :answer/id #uuid "72dc653f-89f3-5bc5-be93-71629ad54c9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115316/selection/7c881a3130cf5ba5f4d7ce51471c0dd9d4b2414dcab4e4043ff888e5db7c5fd3" :answer/id #uuid "266bc01a-57e7-5e89-bd7f-65cbda81a8db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-4,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115316/selection/298289ff2783728b9c035911ec6fe053a7e35464abb98323c2f17c9d57e49b1f" :answer/id #uuid "dc3eb529-1f6a-54d6-8be1-fbbfde367229" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115316/selection/dd7fbe3b8d5c62d67bb1f4ccb0a5e7d1b13c582b15c5893f85139caf3eb799b7" :answer/id #uuid "f9af7107-23dc-5a0b-9b4f-e7e869f834ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115316/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2b48a5e-0fd7-5158-9e35-2801da6ff289" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115316/selection/7c881a3130cf5ba5f4d7ce51471c0dd9d4b2414dcab4e4043ff888e5db7c5fd3" :answer-field/choices ["q-115316/selection/7a5aab969ffcdbe5ac6bd1a68897506c93bac105dd752828cf140c8ec9e1f647" "q-115316/selection/f2b3d4b1886cc4c3079a0c9268e27d63493239a5d6ef9ca8c4a6ace4d05e3e97" "q-115316/selection/7c881a3130cf5ba5f4d7ce51471c0dd9d4b2414dcab4e4043ff888e5db7c5fd3" "q-115316/selection/298289ff2783728b9c035911ec6fe053a7e35464abb98323c2f17c9d57e49b1f" "q-115316/selection/dd7fbe3b8d5c62d67bb1f4ccb0a5e7d1b13c582b15c5893f85139caf3eb799b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115316" :question/id #uuid "130e116d-8ed6-52b7-9583-d268872d4b07" :question/math-academy-id "q-115316" :question/problem "Determine the center of the ellipse whose equation is\n$2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+16x-2y+29=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must group the $x$ terms and the $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+16x-2y+29 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+16x)+({y}^{2}-2y)+29 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}^{2}+16x)+({y}^{2}-2y)+29 & =0 \\\\ 2[{x}^{2}+8x]+[{y}^{2}-2y]+29 & =0 \\\\ 2[(x+4)^{2}-{4}^{2}]+[(y-1)^{2}-{1}^{2}]+29 & =0 \\\\ 2[(x+4)^{2}-16]+[(y-1)^{2}-1]+29 & =0 \\\\ 2(x+4)^{2}-32+(y-1)^{2}-1+29 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+4)^{2}-32+(y-1)^{2}-1+29 & =0 \\\\ 2(x+4)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =32+1-29 \\\\ 2(x+4)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse is centered at $(-4,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115316/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d58fba3c-4bbf-5a74-a911-18db101eb632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115316"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-16565/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "4a5f69d6-fdf0-54c6-886a-f13726e62add" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16565/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "6250a21c-5285-5eab-a621-61f2e4564ea4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16565/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "52df560